-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Precision:** Floating-point precision in step alignment may cause gaps or overlaps in sampling if `step_len` is not a divisor of segment lengths [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Boundaries:** Ensure `row` calculation does not exceed image height [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Degenerate Input:** If `rotation_axis.zero()` in camera setup, handle appropriately [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## Subtopics
 
-### SparseLeap
-Uses sparse voxel octrees for space skipping. Chose when memory efficiency is critical and data is highly sparse. [Link](5152-sparseleap.md)
+### Visibility Culling
+Uses visibility information to skip rays that do not intersect the volume. [Visibility Culling](6226-visibility-culling.md)
 
-### Visibility Culling
-Culls entire tiles or view frustums. Chose when large portions of the volume are outside the view. [Link](6226-visibility-culling.md)
-*   **Efficient Space Skipping & Adaptive Sampling of Unstructured Volumes Using H.W. Accel. Ray Tracing:** Uses hardware-accelerated ray tracing for unstructured volumes. Chose when GPU ray tracing cores are available and data is unstructured. [Link](8217-efficient-space-skipping-adaptive-sampling-of-unstructured-v.md)
-*   **SparseLeap Ray-Casting with Occupancy Misses:** Extends SparseLeap with occupancy misses for further culling. Chose when maximum culling is needed for sparse data. [Link](9818-sparseleap-ray-casting-with-occupancy-misses.md)
+### Bounding Volume Empty-Space Culling
+Uses bounding volumes to cull empty space. [Bounding Volume Empty-Space Culling](17140-bounding-volume-empty-space-culling.md)
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of occupied segments and sampling points per ray. Parallelization reduces wall-clock time by a factor proportional to the number of threads and MPI ranks, subject to communication overhead.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of volume blocks and segments. Precomputed block offsets and segment lists add memory overhead.
+*   **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of active samples. The parallelization reduces wall-clock time by a factor proportional to the number of threads and MPI ranks, subject to communication overhead.
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of voxels and the number of segments. The segment list size depends on the volume's empty space ratio.
 *   **Measured Performance:** Not given in the sources.
-*   **Scaling:** Scales with MPI ranks and OpenMP threads. Communication overhead between ranks may limit scaling for small images or high communication costs.
-*   **Strengths:** Effective for structured brick-based volumes. Simple parallelization strategy.
-*   **Limitations:** Requires precomputation of segment lists. May not be as efficient for highly unstructured or dynamic data as other methods.
-*   **When to Use:** Structured brick-based volumes with significant empty space.
-*   **When Not to Use:** Highly unstructured data, or when memory for segment lists is constrained.
+*   **Scaling:** Scales with the number of MPI ranks and OpenMP threads.
+*   **Strengths:** Efficiently skips empty space, reducing the number of samples per ray. Parallelization improves performance on multi-core and multi-node systems.
+*   **Limitations:** Requires precomputation of segment lists. Performance depends on the efficiency of the segment list generation and the distribution of work across threads.
+*   **When to use:** When rendering large volumes with significant empty space on parallel hardware.
+*   **When not:** When the volume is dense and empty space skipping provides little benefit, or when the overhead of segment list generation is high.
 
 ## Background
-The method is described in the repository `hopexn/VolumeRenderingParallel` [S1, unofficial]. It is an implementation of parallel volume rendering using MPI and OpenMP with segment lists for space skipping.
+Parallel Ray Casting with Segment Lists is described in the repository [hopexn/VolumeRenderingParallel](https://github.com/hopexn/VolumeRenderingParallel) [S1, unofficial]. It uses OpenMP for threading and MPI for distributed rendering.
 
